Changes made by FlashRT (2026-11-15)
  - Renamed analyze-model-impl to vla-model-impl-map. Rewrote the description
    for FlashRT VLA models and added Chinese trigger words.
  - Replaced the ApxInf-specific execution chain (Python AutoPolicy, Rust
    AutoModel/ModelRunner, crates/apxinf-*, C ABI adapters) with FlashRT's
    chain:
      * BackendConfig and registry.validate_config/load_backend;
      * frontends under flash_rt/frontends/torch/;
      * model pipelines under flash_rt/models/<model>/;
      * torch ops versus fvk pybind bindings in csrc/bindings.cpp;
      * GemmRunner/CachedGemmRunner (cuBLASLt);
      * SDPA and FA2 backend selection;
      * CMake architecture gates.
  - Renamed the table columns: "Rust op" / "C ABI / vendor call" / "Selected
    CUDA kernel" became "Python module/function" / "torch op or fvk binding" /
    "Selected kernel/backend". Added a leading "Stage" column.
  - Added stage-id tagging against flash_rt/vla/autotune/stages.py (seams,
    PROFILE_KEYS, stage-map gaps). Positioned the map as the static half of
    stage attribution.
  - Added snapshot-candidate scoping (map the snapshot's source_dir), recording
    of dispatch environment variables, and FlashRT graph-cache and host-sync
    guidance.
  - Changed the report location rule from "follow AGENTS.md" to FlashRT's
    ignored devlocal/<feat>/reports/ directory. Added optional decision-log
    recording.
  - Removed the LLM prefill/decode, expert-routing and output-head specifics
    that do not apply to these VLA models. The method is kept: verify every
    claim against code, separate load from repeated execution, make frequency
    explicit, do not invent kernel symbols, and do not claim runtime
    validation from static analysis.
  - Moved the FlashRT per-model entry points to
    references/flashrt-execution-paths.md.
  - agents/openai.yaml was rewritten for this skill.
